brief:
  - Work only in E:\Source\Rust\TinyRustLM.com on codex/model-acquisition-v2 for TinyRustLM source. Model payloads belong only in D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM; the owner's storage instruction supersedes the old D: prohibition. Leave X:\LLMS untouched.
  - TinyRustLM is prelaunch and clean-slate. Delete superseded implementations after verified replacement; add no compatibility or debt.
  - Read workspace.uai current_companion_truth for current implementation. Production source ownership, acquisition, conversion, terminal inspection, transfer, listener and browser client wiring exist; old checkpoint 5a9c097 is historical.
  - The 47 newest reports are byte-exact, reviewed, ledgered, and routed by the decision index. They are advisory, not execution evidence.
  - MemoryEndpoints direct agent coordination and the TinyRustLM.com Connect user plugin are separate authorized lanes. Synchronized redundant prelaunch memory is allowed.
  - No model, browser, P2P, live memory, deployment, or publication claim exists beyond exact named receipts; counters remain zero.
  - Continue the ecosystem cleanup in docs/ecosystem-cleanup-2026-09-12.md. Record experimental purpose, exact inputs, observed results, useful lessons and uncertainty before retiring obsolete files; use the canonical experiment-lessons record and Git history.
  - Establish an eligible exact model and fresh numerical bindings before real qualification. The unchanged pinned Qwen3 weights remain rejected product ancestry, including byte-identical renamed repositories; see artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/public-source-metadata-review.json.
  - MiniModel.org may provide initial verified server seeds. Restore eligible cache or automatically acquire a small qualified starter, with HF/local/conversion/manual peer controls in Advanced. A real qualified model and the hosting placement decision remain open.
  - Commit and push every coherent green major change; deploy every affected site whenever its complete gate passes.
